# Contractor Copy & Voice

Write for **homeowners ready to hire** — not builders, architects, or trade partners. Every headline, CTA, meta description, and component label should sound like a trusted local remodeler speaking directly to the customer.

## Audience

Homeowners in **Salt Lake County and Utah County** planning a remodel. They care about quality, timeline, budget clarity, and whether they can trust you in their home.

## Voice

- **Confident and approachable** — expert without being condescending
- **Clear over clever** — say what you do and what happens next
- **Reassuring** — reduce remodel anxiety (mess, surprises, delays, budget creep)
- **First person plural** — "we" and "our team"; address the reader as "you" and "your home"

## Industry Language to Use

| Use | Instead of |
|-----|------------|
| remodel / renovation | project (alone), solution, leverage |
| free consultation | inquiry, submit a ticket |
| estimate / quote | pricing request, RFQ |
| on-site assessment / walkthrough | site visit (ok), audit |
| craftsmanship / quality work | best-in-class, synergy |
| timeline / schedule | deliverables, sprint |
| itemized estimate | proposal doc |
| licensed & insured | fully credentialed provider |
| transform / update / finish | optimize, iterate |
| concept to completion | end-to-end lifecycle |

## Trust & Process Phrases

Weave these naturally — don't stack them in one paragraph:

- "Clear communication from start to finish"
- "Itemized estimate — no surprises"
- "Quality craftsmanship you can see"
- "On time and on budget"
- "We work in your home like it's our own"
- "From first walkthrough to final walkthrough"

## Service Terminology

Match how homeowners search and speak:

- **Kitchen remodel** — countertops, cabinets, backsplash, layout
- **Bathroom remodel** — vanity, tile, shower, fixtures
- **Basement finish / basement remodel** — finish-out, living space, home office
- **Fireplace install** — electric fireplace, built-in, surround

## CTAs

Action-oriented, low-commitment first step:

```tsx
// ✅ GOOD
"Schedule a Free Consultation"
"Request an Estimate"
"Tell Us About Your Project"

// ❌ BAD
"Learn More" (too vague)
"Submit" (cold)
"Get Started Today!" (hypey)
```

## Words to Avoid

- Corporate SaaS: leverage, streamline, ecosystem, scalable, disrupt
- Vague superlatives: world-class, premier, leading (unless backed by proof)
- Unexplained trade jargon: rough-in, jack stud, LVL (homeowners won't search these)
- Fear-based selling: "Don't hire the wrong contractor"

## Examples

```tsx
// ❌ BAD
"We provide comprehensive renovation solutions for residential clients."

// ✅ GOOD
"We handle kitchen and bathroom remodels, basement finish-outs, and fireplace installs — with clear estimates and a timeline you can count on."
```

```tsx
// ❌ BAD — metadata
description: "Home improvement services in Utah."

// ✅ GOOD — metadata
description: "Kitchen & bathroom remodels in Salt Lake City and Utah County. Free on-site consultation. Quality craftsmanship, clear estimates, on-time completion."
```
